<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">maul</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">maul</ansi> command drives your natural fangs into your opponent
in a savage tearing flurry, worrying the wound. It deals heavy
damage and applies a stronger bleeding condition on a successful
strike than rake.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must have natural fangs (fanged species only)
  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">maul</ansi>
  Attempt to maul your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Heavy. The savage bite deals significant harm.
  <ansi fg="stat">Bleed:</ansi> A successful maul opens deep wounds that bleed
    severely over several rounds, dealing substantial additional
    damage beyond the initial strike.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with other special moves.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Maul spends Stamina and requires full payment before the strike. Carried load
raises the price, while <ansi fg="skill">unarmed-combat</ansi> skill lowers it.
If you are too spent, no cooldown, combat round, or effect is consumed.

Maul's heavy damage and persistent deep bleed make it a potent
finisher for wearing down prey over a sustained fight. See
<ansi fg="command">help conditions</ansi> for details on the bleeding effect.

